Adaptations: native Go transport, github.com/flynn/noise XX handshake and cipher states, bounded device
API requests, paired credential-file persistence, cancellation-aware directory
serialization and explicit uncertain-send classification. The Muse-specific
2^53-1 nonce ceiling and fatal authentication failure policy wrap the Noise
library; the official SDK fixed-byte fixtures establish wire compatibility.

The existing muse-client 0.1.0 TypeScript package was inspected as an unofficial
reference for Relanox's prior behavior. It is not a runtime dependency.
Local protocol validation does not establish live Muse account compatibility.
